# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
# `.claude/*` denies EVERYTHING under `.claude/`, so local-only state
# (settings.local.json, scheduled_tasks.lock) stays out of the repo by default.
# Every directory that must be committed needs its own `!.claude/<dir>/` line
# immediately below. A new subdirectory added WITHOUT one is invisible to git
# and to CI — `git add -A` silently skips it, and every test asserting over it
# passes vacuously rather than failing. Verify with `git check-ignore -v <path>`:
# exit 1 means the path is committable, exit 0 names the denying rule.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/lanes/

